[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Hypervisor ABI and Partition Isolation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-HYP-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Minimal Eight-Hypercall ABI Surface
STATEMENT: >>>
The bare-metal Type-1 hypervisor shall expose a bounded ABI of at most eight hypercalls: Yield, WaitEvent, Notify, TimeRead, FaultReport, SlotOp, PartCtl, and DiagTrace, with zero payload-copying message syscalls inside the hypervisor kernel.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Keeping the hypervisor call surface minimal and data-plane-free minimizes the Class B kernel code size and enables 100 percent MC/DC structural coverage.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Inspection
ARTIFACT: hypervisor/include/strata/hyp/abi.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-HYP-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Deterministic Minor and Major Frame Time Partitioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The hypervisor shall schedule partitions according to a static build-time minor/major cyclic frame table, preempting any partition immediately upon exhaustion of its minor-frame execution budget without jitter leakage into higher-criticality partitions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Strict temporal partitioning guarantees deterministic real-time deadlines for flight-critical C&DH, comms, and FDIR partitions regardless of payload workload.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: hypervisor/include/strata/hyp/hypervisor.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-HYP-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Hardware Spatial Memory and Peripheral Isolation
STATEMENT: >>>
The hypervisor shall enforce static, non-overlapping memory and MMIO mappings per partition via hardware Stage-2 MMU (AArch64 EL2), MPU (Cortex-R5F / MicroBlaze), and external memory/bus protection units (XMPU/SMMU), granting Read-Only mappings to shared consumer regions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Hardware memory enforcement guarantees that a wild pointer or corrupted DMA descriptor in a lower-criticality partition cannot alter another partition's memory or registers.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: hypervisor/include/strata/hyp/hypervisor.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-HYP-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Hypervisor-Enforced Doorbell Token-Bucket Rate Limiting
STATEMENT: >>>
The hypervisor shall enforce a per-channel static authorization check and token-bucket rate budget on every Notify hypercall, throttling excessive inter-partition doorbells before delivering hardware IPIs.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A runaway guest looping on doorbell notifications could otherwise cause an interrupt storm that starves a Class B receiving partition.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: hypervisor/include/strata/hyp/hypervisor.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-HYP-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Monotonic Partition and Slot Generation Counters
STATEMENT: >>>
The hypervisor shall maintain a monotonic 16-bit generation identifier (GenId) for every partition and hardware slot, incrementing the counter upon every restart or reload so peer partitions immediately detect stale handles and in-flight transactions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Explicit generation counters eliminate subtle race conditions and hung IPC transactions when a peer partition restarts asynchronously.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: hypervisor/include/strata/hyp/abi.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-HYP-006
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Warm Restart CriticalStore Preservation and Cold Restart Scrub
STATEMENT: >>>
On a privileged PartCtl(WarmRestart) invocation, the hypervisor shall halt the target partition, zero its stack and .bss memory, preserve its dedicated CriticalStore checkpoint region, increment its GenId, and re-enter the partition in WarmStart mode; on ColdRestart it shall additionally clear the CriticalStore region.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Distinguishing warm and cold partition restarts enables sub-2 ms autonomous state recovery after transient upsets while providing a clean cold-boot reset path.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: hypervisor/include/strata/hyp/hypervisor.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-HYP-007
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Read-Only Shared Hardware Time Page
STATEMENT: >>>
The hypervisor shall map a cache-line-aligned 64-byte Read-Only SharedTimePage into every partition, updated via Seqlock from the static hardware 1PPS and TAI counter so partitions read nanosecond TAI time without trapping into the hypervisor.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Zero-trap shared time reads eliminate syscall latency jitter and keep all CPU partitions synchronized to the exact same hardware TAI epoch used by PL slots.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: hypervisor/include/strata/hyp/abi.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-HYP-008
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Privileged Trap Capture and Out-of-Kernel Supervisor Policy
STATEMENT: >>>
The hypervisor shall trap hardware exceptions (data/instruction abort, alignment fault, undefined instruction, privilege violation) and FaultReport calls, halt the offending partition, capture diagnostic register state (PC, LR, fault syndrome, fault address, GenId), and notify the unprivileged FDIR supervisor partition rather than hardcoding recovery policy in kernel mode.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Separating fault containment (hypervisor) from mission recovery policy (FDIR supervisor) keeps the privileged kernel tiny, deterministic, and mission-independent.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: hypervisor/include/strata/hyp/hypervisor.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-HYP-009
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Multi-Architecture Hypervisor Backends
STATEMENT: >>>
The hypervisor shall implement clean architecture backends under the shared 8-hypcall ABI for Versal Cortex-A72 (EL2), Versal Lockstep Cortex-R5F (MPU + PMC PLM/XilSEM bridge), Kintex TMR MicroBlaze (external rad-hard supervisor bridge), and a deterministic host SIL simulation backend.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Isolating architecture-specific trap, MMU, and IPI code behind a unified core allows seamless portability across Versal, Kintex, and desktop SIL environments.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Demonstration
ARTIFACT: hypervisor/arch/host_sil/host_sil_backend.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-002

[[/SECTION]]
